  "articleBody": "Choosing between tile and luxury vinyl flooring comes down to how your household uses the kitchen and what maintenance you prefer. Both options handle foot traffic, but they perform differently across daily wear, subfloor requirements, and project schedules.\n\nTile offers unmatched durability and high moisture resistance. Ceramic, porcelain, and stone handle major spills without warping. However, tile requires a completely rigid subfloor to prevent grout cracking, takes three to five days to install due to thinset and grout curing, and feels harder underfoot. Luxury vinyl installs faster, often wrapping up in one to two days, and provides softer underfoot comfort. While vinyl resists top-down spills easily, standing water that seeps beneath floating seams can compromise subfloors if neglected. \n\nHow to Compare Your Options\nLook closely at your existing subfloor and installation timeline. If you have an uneven timber subfloor on an older home, luxury vinyl may require less structural reinforcement, whereas tile requires thorough leveling and uncoupling membranes. If you want maximum scratch resistance against pets or dropped cookware, porcelain tile remains the sturdier choice. \n\nWhen your project involves adjusting floor heights against cabinetry or leveling a sloping subfloor, hiring an experienced installer ensures the foundation holds up. Contact Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to discuss your kitchen flooring options.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
